Hi Folks,

the patch-2.6.6-mh1 is almost ready and it includes a prototype of the
upcoming HIDP support. In conjunction with the hidd program from the
bluez-utils-2.7 release it gives a forecast of the final Bluetooth HID
support for Linux. However I put the patch on hold until tomorrow,
because I want to include some USB related fixes for the oopses people
had seen with enabled SCO support. So check out www.bluez.org and look
for a news entry with that topic.

Regards

Marcel




